# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) to point the SPA at a real backend instead of
# the built-in mock adapter (see src/api/client.ts / src/api/mock.ts).
#
# Without this set, `npm run dev` silently falls back to `mockClient`: every
# screen renders fully populated seeded demo data (a sample transcript, GPA,
# programs, alerts) instead of your real (or empty) record. Look for the
# "Demo data" banner in the app shell (frontend/src/layouts/AppLayout.tsx) —
# if you see it, you are NOT talking to a live backend.
#
# Production builds (`npm run build`) default to `/api` even without this file
# (src/api/client.ts), since Flask serves the SPA same-origin in production.
#
# Recommended for dev (Codespaces included): vite.config.ts ships a
# `server.proxy` that forwards /api/* to a Flask backend on localhost:5000,
# so the relative path Just Works with `npm run dev`:
VITE_API_BASE=/api
#
# Backend on a different host/port (no proxy)? Point at it directly instead:
# VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:5000/api
